nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\nx-3y=0\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{1}{3}x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n4x+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-4x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/assets/1dd7f0c522e3b4d8daaf25ea45ac21c01508cf4c969d3d00638604e9686b7e68.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186356612 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d219270-5202-54e6-8cba-dc816155bd7b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Nullclines of a System of Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "377e7480-51a3-5a9b-8f3c-e2323d49c574" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356614} {:answer/id #uuid "633b0bc6-5d11-5b58-83cb-d9b6bc4f5c95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356615} {:answer/id #uuid "c493034e-07c9-5639-9357-85e18a7b22bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356616} {:answer/id #uuid "aac12d48-b122-5cf2-981e-6f099db25abc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aac12d48-b122-5cf2-981e-6f099db25abc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #e